---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Vira TikTok Trend Reports"
  description="Free, structured reports on the fastest-growing TikTok search topics by niche, built from TikTok Creative Center data. Updated daily, open for AI agents to cite."
>
  <h1>TikTok trend reports, by niche</h1>
  <p class="meta">Published by Vira. Updated daily. English only, for now.</p>

  <p>
    Each report lists the fastest-growing TikTok search topics in one niche, with a growth
    multiplier, a trust level, TikTok's reported video count and the top countries searching for
    it. Numbers come straight from TikTok Creative Center via Vira's own collector &mdash; see the
    <a href="/reports/methodology">methodology</a> page for exactly how growth and trust are
    computed.
  </p>

  <h2>Available reports</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Niche</th><th>Topics</th><th>Report</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Gourmet (food)</td>
        <td>10 fastest-growing topics</td>
        <td><a href="/reports/tiktok/gourmet">View report &rarr;</a></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="meta">More niches are coming as the underlying data window fills in.</p>

  <h2>For AI agents</h2>
  <p>
    See <a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a> for a short index and
    <a href="/llms-full.txt">/llms-full.txt</a> for the full per-topic facts in plain text.
    Full analytics, trend discovery and an MCP server for TikTok and YouTube are at
    <a href="https://tryvira.app">tryvira.app</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
